/T (Why the PCA9685 Chip? The STM32 does not have 18 PWM output pins available. The PCA9685 chip connects over just two wires \(I2C: SDA + SCL\) and generates 16 independent PWM signals on its own oscillator. The STM32 sends all 18 angles in one 73-byte I2C burst, taking about 1.6 ms.)
/E (Why the PCA9685 Chip? The STM32 does not have 18 PWM output pins available. The PCA9685 chip connects over just two wires \(I2C: SDA + SCL\) and generates 16 independent PWM signals on its own oscillator. The STM32 sends all 18 angles in one 73-byte I2C burst, taking about 1.6 ms.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
